WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.607
Model Context Protocol security is about protecting the integration path between AI applications and the outside systems they can reach.

2
00:00:09.607 --> 00:00:16.586
MCP makes it easier for an AI host to connect to tools, resources, prompts, data stores, and services.

3
00:00:16.586 --> 00:00:19.952
That usefulness changes the security boundary.

4
00:00:19.952 --> 00:00:30.954
A model response is no longer only text on a screen; it may lead to a tool call, a file read, an API request, a ticket update, or another action in a real environment.

5
00:00:30.954 --> 00:00:36.784
At a high level, an MCP host is the AI application or environment where the user works.

6
00:00:36.784 --> 00:00:40.807
An MCP client is the component that speaks to an MCP server.

7
00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:44.256
The server exposes tools, resources, or prompts.

8
00:00:44.256 --> 00:00:46.883
A tool is an action the system can call.

9
00:00:46.883 --> 00:00:50.250
A resource is data the system can read or present.

10
00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.616
Prompt templates can shape how tasks are framed.

11
00:00:53.616 --> 00:00:55.587
Transports carry messages.

12
00:00:55.587 --> 00:01:05.193
Downstream systems are the APIs, files, databases, cloud services, and workflow platforms that ultimately provide data or perform work.

13
00:01:05.193 --> 00:01:07.985
MCP security is not only model security.

14
00:01:07.985 --> 00:01:13.732
Prompt wording can help guide behavior, but it is not a reliable security boundary.

15
00:01:13.732 --> 00:01:26.459
The important controls live across application security, identity, authorization, data protection, tool governance, supply-chain review, logging, monitoring, and operations.

16
00:01:26.459 --> 00:01:37.379
A secure design asks what the model can see, what tools it can call, which identity those calls use, what data can move, and what actions can change real systems.

17
00:01:37.379 --> 00:01:42.880
Useful MCP systems must be bounded, authorized, observable, and recoverable.

18
00:01:42.880 --> 00:01:46.575
Bounded means tools and resources have clear limits.

19
00:01:46.575 --> 00:01:52.733
Authorized means permissions come from policy and identity, not from model confidence.

20
00:01:52.733 --> 00:01:59.138
Observable means tool calls, denials, approvals, and resource access can be investigated.

21
00:01:59.138 --> 00:02:05.378
Recoverable means high-impact actions have rollback plans and incident response paths.

22
00:02:05.378 --> 00:02:12.028
The goal is not to block MCP adoption; it is to make powerful integrations safe enough to operate.
